#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:243
msgid "A floating label sits inside the empty field like a placeholder and moves to the top edge, smaller, as soon as the field is focused or filled. The plugin rebuilds the markup Contact Form 7 renders and ships the stylesheet; your pages need no JavaScript for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:244
msgid "Text, email, URL, telephone, number, date, textarea and select fields get floating labels. The label of a date field stays floated, because browsers show a format mask in the empty field; the label of a select stays floated too, except while its blank option is selected. Checkboxes, radio buttons, selects with multiple choice, file uploads, quizzes and CAPTCHAs keep their original markup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:245
msgid "The label text comes from the form template (a <label> that encloses the field or points at its id) or from the placeholder option of the form-tag. A label in the template wins over a placeholder. With the option \"Text before the field\", loose text in front of the field, or in the paragraph just before it, is used when there is neither; that covers the default template of Contact Form 7 before version 5.4."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:246
msgid "Fields the plugin does not recognise are left exactly as Contact Form 7 renders them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:247
msgid "The stylesheet follows the loading policy of Contact Form 7, which loads it on every page. Tick \"Only on pages with a form\" under \"Stylesheet\" to load it on single posts and pages with a form only; a form rendered elsewhere still gets it, late in the footer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:248
msgid "The box \"Sample page\" at the top of this screen creates a private page with forms that show the options, and removes it again together with its forms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:257
msgid "The settings of this screen apply to every form. Override them per form, per placement or per field; later layers win."
msgstr ""

