#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:509
msgid "Where the text of a floating label comes from. All sources can be active: a label in the form template wins over a placeholder, and loose text is used only when there is neither."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:518
msgid "Only fields of these Contact Form 7 types get a floating label. The label of a date field stays floated (browsers show a format mask), and so does the label of a select, except while its blank option is selected. Checkboxes, radio buttons, selects with multiple choice, files and quizzes never get one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:527
msgid "Colours, sizes and timing of the fields. Leave a field empty to keep the default; only the values you change are printed, as CSS custom properties on the .wpcf7 wrapper, right after the stylesheet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:543
msgid "Use the text of a label in the form template"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:544
msgid "The <label> that encloses the field, as in the default template, or a <label for=\"...\"> that points at the id of the field."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:551
msgid "Use the placeholder of the field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:552
msgid "The placeholder option of the form-tag becomes the label text; the placeholder itself is replaced by a single space."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:559
msgid "Use loose text in front of the field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:560
msgid "For templates without a label and without a placeholder, such as the default template of Contact Form 7 before version 5.4: the text right in front of the field, or the paragraph just before it, becomes the label text. A heuristic, off by default; check the result and add the option nofloat to fields that should keep their text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:579
msgid "Load the stylesheet of the plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:580
msgid "Untick when your theme styles the classes jgor-flcf7-* itself; the design values below are then not printed either. The stylesheet follows the loading policy of Contact Form 7."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:584
msgid "Only on pages with a form"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:585
msgid "Contact Form 7 loads its stylesheet on every page, and so does this plugin by default. Tick to load it only on single posts and pages whose content holds the Contact Form 7 block or shortcode. A form rendered elsewhere, for example in a widget, a template part or an archive, still gets the stylesheet, but late in the footer, so it may show unstyled for a moment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:592
msgid "Append an asterisk to the label of required fields"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:593
msgid "Shown through CSS behind the label of fields with aria-required=\"true\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:600
msgid "Shown on the submit button, in the error colour, while the form has validation errors; the label of each invalid field floats up and the message appears inside the field. Leave empty to change only the colour of the button."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:605
msgid "Pick a colour or leave the field empty to keep the default shown as \"Default\" in the picker. The Filled variant uses a light grey, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06), as its default background."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:609
#: assets/js/block-editor.js:167
msgid "A number with px, em, rem or %, for example 0.9em. The font size of the field also scales the label and the padding; 1em keeps the size of the surrounding text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:613
#: assets/js/block-editor.js:173
msgid "Scale of the floated label between 0.5 and 1; duration of the transitions with s or ms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:617
